{
  /**
   * CANONICAL TypeScript configuration for the Qwik City storefront.
   * Editors, `tsc --noEmit` (the `typecheck` script) and CI all read this file.
   *
   * MODULE STRATEGY — the NodeNext alignment contract:
   *
   * `module: NodeNext` + `moduleResolution: NodeNext` is mandated so this app
   * type-checks `@moringa/sdk` sources under exactly the same resolution rules
   * the NestJS backend ecosystem publishes. Because this package deliberately
   * omits `"type": "module"` (mirroring the backend), every `.ts/.tsx` here is
   * analysed as a CommonJS-flavoured unit:
   *
   *   - extensionless relative imports stay valid (`./shop`, not `./shop.js`),
   *     so the existing route/component tree needs zero import churn;
   *   - bare specifiers resolve through `node_modules` with full support for
   *     modern `exports` maps (`@nestia/fetcher` v13 ships import/require
   *     conditions that `node10` resolution cannot even express);
   *   - the workspace-linked SDK resolves through its package `main`/`types`
   *     pointing at raw `.ts` sources, giving instant cross-project
   *     autocomplete and compile errors when backend endpoints change.
   *
   * Emission is owned by Vite/Rollup (client) and the Qwik optimizer (SSR);
   * `tsc` runs strictly as the type oracle (`noEmit`). The single sanctioned
   * escape hatch for Vite's `import.meta.env` lives in `src/lib/env.ts`.
   */
  "extends": "../../tsconfig.base.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    /* ---- module contract (see block comment above) ---- */
    "module": "NodeNext",
    "moduleResolution": "NodeNext",

    /* ---- language level ---- */
    "target": "ES2022",
    "lib": ["ES2022", "DOM", "DOM.Iterable"],
    "jsx": "react-jsx",
    "jsxImportSource": "@builder.io/qwik",

    /* ---- correctness gates ---- */
    "strict": true,
    "noImplicitOverride": true,
    "noFallthroughCasesInSwitch": true,
    "forceConsistentCasingInFileNames": true,
    "allowJs": false,
    "isolatedModules": true,

    /* ---- interop & tooling ---- */
    "esModuleInterop": true,
    "resolveJsonModule": true,
    "skipLibCheck": true,
    "types": ["node", "vite/client"],

    /* ---- no emission: Vite owns output ---- */
    "noEmit": true,

    /* ---- workspace path mappings ----
     * Declared WITHOUT baseUrl: since TypeScript 5.0, relative `paths` are
     * resolved against THIS config file's directory. These mappings pin the
     * workspace packages to their raw TypeScript entry points so a backend
     * endpoint change surfaces as an error HERE at type-check time — before
     * any runtime request can drift from the generated contract.
     *
     * The three `@builder.io/qwik*` entries are NodeNext-compat pins, not
     * redirects: Qwik 1.x's dist/jsx-runtime.d.ts re-exports via extensionless
     * relative specifiers (`from './core'`), which are illegal when that
     * declaration file is analyzed as ESM under nodenext (the file itself
     * comments "when not using nodenext import resolution"). skipLibCheck
     * hides the internal error but the JSX namespace then fails to load,
     * producing TS7026 on every element. Pinning the jsx factory modules to
     * dist/core.d.ts — the exact file Qwik's own exports map already names
     * for "." types — restores full JSX.IntrinsicElements typing under pure
     * NodeNext with zero runtime impact (Vite emits its own factory imports). */
    "paths": {
      "@builder.io/qwik": ["../../node_modules/@builder.io/qwik/dist/core.d.ts"],
      "@builder.io/qwik/jsx-runtime": [
        "../../node_modules/@builder.io/qwik/dist/core.d.ts"
      ],
      /* Same class of NodeNext-compat pin as Qwik above: Vite 6 exposes its
       * CJS build via "./index.cjs" with no adjacent declarations, so tsc
       * under nodenext cannot attach defineConfig/UserConfig/Plugin. Pinning
       * to the canonical node API surface restores full typing. */
      "vite": ["../../node_modules/vite/dist/node/index.d.ts"],
      "@moringa/sdk": ["../../libs/sdk/src/index.ts"],
      "@moringa/sdk/*": ["../../libs/sdk/src/*"],
      "@moringa/shared": ["../../libs/shared/src/index.ts"],
      "@moringa/shared/*": ["../../libs/shared/src/*"]
    }
  },
  "include": [
    "src/**/*.ts",
    "src/**/*.tsx",
    "./*.config.ts"
  ],
  "exclude": [
    "node_modules",
    "dist",
    "server",
    "tmp",
    "**/*.spec.ts",
    "**/*.test.ts"
  ]
}
